WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.327 --> 00:00:12.735
This final lesson is for group owners, who run more than one organisation, such as Robokalam, Samaritan Stand-Up, Calvings and Nextpreneur, from a single place.

2
00:00:13.596 --> 00:00:34.044
Each organisation in KalamDesk has its own people, tasks, scores, leads, expenses and dashboard. Nobody in one organisation can see anything from another. Only group owners, who are founders of every organisation, can move between them.

3
00:00:34.903 --> 00:00:43.735
At the top of the left menu is the organisation switcher. It shows where you are. Click it.

4
00:00:44.596 --> 00:00:56.524
Choose another organisation, for example Samaritan Stand-Up. The whole screen changes: its own people, its own tasks, and its own colour.

5
00:00:57.392 --> 00:01:08.360
Look at the Desk. Only Samaritan's team is here, and the app is painted in its colour. Nothing from Robokalam is visible.

6
00:01:09.221 --> 00:01:18.269
Click People to confirm. Only people in this organisation are listed, together with you, as their founder.

7
00:01:19.134 --> 00:01:30.054
To manage all your organisations, open the switcher again, and click Manage organisations. Or choose Organisations in the menu.

8
00:01:30.926 --> 00:01:54.278
Each organisation has a card with its number of people and open tasks. Open takes you inside it. Edit lets you rename it, change its description, and pick its brand colour. Archive hides an organisation, and signs its people out. Nothing is deleted, and you can restore it.

9
00:01:55.144 --> 00:01:59.944
To start a new organisation, click New organisation.

10
00:02:00.802 --> 00:02:19.642
Type its name. Choose a brand colour. Optionally, enter the name and email of its first founder, who will receive an invitation, and will only ever see this organisation. Then click Create. We will cancel this one.

11
00:02:20.504 --> 00:02:35.384
Further down, Group owners lists the founders who can open every organisation. You can grant or remove that access with one click. Other founders stay limited to their own organisation.

12
00:02:36.248 --> 00:02:54.656
Remember: an email address belongs to only one organisation. If someone works for two, give them a separate email for each, or make them a group owner. Each time you sign in, you start back in your home organisation.

13
00:02:55.514 --> 00:03:07.466
That completes the KalamDesk lessons. Keep the written user guide handy, and ask your founder if anything is unclear. Thank you for watching.
